<title>USA: Dotronix receives pilot order for displays.</title>
<headline>Dotronix receives pilot order for displays.</headline>
<dateline>NEW BRIGHTON, Minn. 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dotronix Inc, maker of high resolution video displays, said Wednesday it had received a pilot run order for 50 high resolution television displays.</p>
<p>Through a leasing company, the displays will be installed in &quot;a major East Coast stock exchange,&quot; Dotronix said, adding that it didn't have permission to name the exchange.</p>
<p>Potential sales for the exchange are more than $2 million, Dotronix said.</p>
<p>Dotronix shares closed down 1/32 at one Wednesday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
